{#
Links for functions to manage NLs.
#}

{% set syncNls = path('nlpservices.sync_nls_form') %}
{% set displayNls = path('nlpservices.display_nls_form') %}
{% set fixes = path('nlpservices.legislative_fixes_form') %}
{% set remindUser = path('nlpservices.login_credentials_reminder_form') %}
{% set mcid = path('nlpservices.reassign_mcid_form') %}


{% trans %}

    <h1>Keep track of NLs</h1>

    <ul>
        <li><a href={{ displayNls }}>Display the list of active NLs.</a></li>
        <li><a href={{ syncNls }}>Sync a new list of active NLs.</a></li>
        <li><a href={{ remindUser }}>Send an email to an NL with a login reminder.</a></li>

    </ul>

    <h1>Correct faulty legislative district information for an NL.</h1>

    <p>Information about NLs is kept in the MyCampaign database of VoteBuilder.   The address is occasionally wrong as
    is the geolocation of that address.  Either case keeps VoteBuilder from identifying the legislative districts
    where the NL lives.   You will see this in the display above as having NLs in HD 0.   If you see this, you should
    first check the validity of the address in MyCampaign.  If it is correct, you can provide substitute legislative
    districts for the NL using the function below. </p>

    <ul>
        <li><a href={{ fixes }}>Define substitutions for missing NL legislative districts.</a></li>
    </ul>


    <h1>Reassign the ID for an NL.</h1>

    <p>This function provides recovery of history information about and NL when the primary MCID was
    destroyed by a merge of a duplicate record in VoteBuilder.   You need to know the original MCID
    that was destroyed and the new MCID that is now associated with the NL.</p>

    <ul>
        <li><a href={{ mcid }}>Reassign the ID associated with an NL.</a></li>
    </ul>


{% endtrans %}
